The two remaining routes do not clear the combined gates. On complete grids, Lemmas 1–2 give the same short arithmetic computation a solver would use, so there is no Track B compression gap. On holey grids, Theorem 1 can carry a degree-3 Vertex Cover certificate into a routing, but its explicit routing certificate already has billions of edge occurrences for an eight-vertex cubic source; replacing it by the short row-cover certificate leaves the solver with Vertex Cover, and the paper proves only worst-case hardness—not hardness for an inverse-planted distribution. I’m recording this as a STEP 0 rejection with both cost comparisons and the exact theorem references.
